FORWARD[symbol][state]:
  sym 0 (0, 1, 3, 2)
  sym 1 (2, 3, 1, 0)
  sym 2 (3, 2, 1, 0)
  sym 3 (3, 2, 1, 0)
INVERSE[symbol][state]:
  sym 0 (0, 1, 3, 2)
  sym 1 (3, 2, 0, 1)
  sym 2 (3, 2, 1, 0)
  sym 3 (3, 2, 1, 0)
BOUNDARY = (3, 2, 1, 0)
CONE[l][r]:
  l = 0 (0, 1, 3, 2)
  l = 1 (3, 2, 1, 0)
  l = 2 (3, 2, 0, 1)
  l = 3 (3, 2, 1, 0)

CONE[1] == CONE[3]: True
swap: (0, 2, 1, 3)

fibres of l -> CONE[l][r] at fixed r (the merge mechanism):
  r=0: images [0, 3, 3, 3]  distinct 2  fibres {0: [0], 3: [1, 2, 3]}
  r=1: images [1, 2, 2, 2]  distinct 2  fibres {1: [0], 2: [1, 2, 3]}
  r=2: images [3, 1, 0, 1]  distinct 3  fibres {0: [2], 1: [1, 3], 3: [0]}
  r=3: images [2, 0, 1, 0]  distinct 3  fibres {0: [1, 3], 1: [2], 2: [0]}

rows of CONE are permutations (r -> CONE[l][r]):
  l=0: [0, 1, 3, 2]  distinct 4
  l=1: [3, 2, 1, 0]  distinct 4
  l=2: [3, 2, 0, 1]  distinct 4
  l=3: [3, 2, 1, 0]  distinct 4

